<title>JAPAN: Japan forgoes buying Australia barley due to price.</title>
<headline>Japan forgoes buying Australia barley due to price.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said it did not buy any Australian barley at Thursday's import tender due to higher-than-expected prices, although it declined to say what the offer price was.</p>
<p>The agency had been planning to buy 20,000 tonnes of feed barley from Australia, an agency official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales prices from Australian exporters were higher than we had expected. We'll try to buy the barley next week,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
